.SH "HISTORY"
Created as a companion to \fBtrace\.sh\fR to work around the limitation that Bash functions cannot be called recursively with a consistent process space\. By externalising the recursion into a separate script, each recursive step runs in its own process, allowing the traversal to descend to arbitrary depth without corrupting shared shell state\.
